<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Kumanovo</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Kumanovo is a city in the north of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/north-macedonia">North Macedonia</a>, near the Serbian border. In the 14th century its district belonged to the Serbian <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/magnates">magnate</a> Dejan and his sons, the Dejanović lords, before Ottoman rule. In October 1912, during the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-balkan-war">First Balkan War</a>, the Serbian army defeated the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottomans</a> at the Battle of Kumanovo, and in 1999 an agreement signed there ended the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kosovo">Kosovo</a> War.</p></div>
